  "problem": "The resting heart rate of a group of adults is normally distributed with a mean of $\\mu \\,\\text{bpm}$ and a standard deviation of $8\\,\\text{bpm}.$ Additionally, $70%$ of the adults have a resting heart rate between $0.9\\mu \\,\\text{bpm}$ and $1.1\\mu \\,\\text{bpm}.$ Find the percentage of adults with a resting heart rate lower than $70\\,\\text{bpm}.$ **Round your answer to two decimal places.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.75\\,$ | $\\,0.80\\,$ | $\\,0.85\\,$ | $\\,0.90\\,$ | $\\,0.95\\,$ | $\\,0.99\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=\u03a6(z)$*.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0359\\,$ | $\\,0.0351\\,$ | $\\,0.0344\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.0446\\,$ | $\\,0.0436\\,$ | $\\,0.0427\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.0548\\,$ | $\\,0.0537\\,$ | $\\,0.0526\\,$ |\n\nApproximately\n{{field-1}}$%$ of the adults have a resting heart rate lower than $70\\,\\text{bpm}.$",
